{\b RTI HomeKit Bridge Driver}

This driver connects to your RTI system via WebSocket and discovers system variables that can be used for HomeKit integration.

{\b Setup Instructions:}

1. {\b Configure RTI Server Settings:}
   - Set the RTI Server Address to your RTI system IP (default: 192.168.102.232)
   - Set the RTI Server Port to the WebSocket port (default: 1234)
   - Verify the WebSocket Endpoint is correct (default: /diagnosticswss)

2. {\b Configure Variable Discovery:}
   - Set the Start Variable ID and End Variable ID range to scan
   - Adjust the Discovery Timeout as needed (default: 3 seconds)
   - Enable Auto Discover Variables to automatically scan on startup

3. {\b Using the Driver:}
   - The driver will automatically connect to your RTI system
   - Use "Discover Variables" to scan for available system variables
   - View discovered variables in the "Discovered Variables" category
   - Use "Export Variable Mapping" to get a JSON mapping of variables

{\b Functions Available:}

{\b Connection Control:}
- Connect: Manually connect to RTI system
- Disconnect: Disconnect from RTI system
- Reconnect: Reconnect to RTI system

{\b Variable Discovery:}
- Discover Variables: Scan for system variables
- Refresh All Variables: Re-subscribe to all discovered variables
- Clear Discovered Variables: Clear the discovered variable list

{\b Variable Control:}
- Subscribe to Variable: Subscribe to a specific variable ID
- Unsubscribe from Variable: Unsubscribe from a specific variable ID
- Test Variable Range: Test the configured variable range

{\b HomeKit Integration:}
- Start HomeKit Bridge: Start the HomeKit bridge (requires Python script)
- Stop HomeKit Bridge: Stop the HomeKit bridge
- Export Variable Mapping: Export variable mapping for HomeKit integration

{\b Debug Functions:}
- Show Connection Status: Display connection information
- Show Discovered Variables: List all discovered variables
- Show WebSocket Log: Display WebSocket message statistics

{\b Troubleshooting:}

- If connection fails, check the RTI server address and port
- Enable debug trace to see detailed logging
- Use "Show Connection Status" to verify connection
- Check "Last WebSocket Message" for recent activity

{\b HomeKit Integration:}

Once variables are discovered, use the exported mapping with the Python HomeKit bridge script to create HomeKit accessories for your RTI devices.

